### Manual checks (VS Code / BAS "REST Client"). Start the app first: cds watch
### Users (mocked, local only): rita/raj = Requester, sam = DataSteward, aud = Auditor, mixa = both roles

@host = http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/mdcr
@nordlicht = 11111111-0000-4000-8000-000000000001
@nordlichtAddr = 22222222-0000-4000-8000-000000000001

### 1. Read suppliers (as auditor)
GET {{host}}/Suppliers?$expand=addresses
Authorization: Basic aud:aud

### 2. Create a change request as a draft (as rita) -> copy the ID from the response
POST {{host}}/ChangeRequests
Authorization: Basic rita:rita
Content-Type: application/json

{ "supplier_ID": "{{nordlicht}}", "address_ID": "{{nordlichtAddr}}",
  "reason": "Postal code has only 4 digits",
  "items": [ { "field": "postalCode", "newValue": "69190" } ] }

### 3. Save it (draft activation) — paste the ID
@id = PASTE-ID-HERE
POST {{host}}/ChangeRequests(ID={{id}},IsActiveEntity=false)/MasterDataService.draftActivate
Authorization: Basic rita:rita
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 4. Submit (as rita) — run it twice: the second time must give 409
POST {{host}}/ChangeRequests(ID={{id}},IsActiveEntity=true)/MasterDataService.submit
Authorization: Basic rita:rita
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 5. Try to approve as the requester -> 403 (wrong role)
POST {{host}}/ChangeRequests(ID={{id}},IsActiveEntity=true)/MasterDataService.approve
Authorization: Basic rita:rita
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 6. Approve as the data steward -> 200, then check the address in request 1
POST {{host}}/ChangeRequests(ID={{id}},IsActiveEntity=true)/MasterDataService.approve
Authorization: Basic sam:sam
Content-Type: application/json

{ "note": "Checked against the invoice letterhead" }

### 7. Invalid postal code for DE -> 400 (create draft, then activate it)
POST {{host}}/ChangeRequests
Authorization: Basic rita:rita
Content-Type: application/json

{ "supplier_ID": "{{nordlicht}}", "address_ID": "{{nordlichtAddr}}",
  "reason": "Wrong fix", "items": [ { "field": "postalCode", "newValue": "6919X" } ] }
